Subject: [PATCH 0005] Statistical .param drawn once per circuit load

Backport of upstream ngspice commit 940bb50fab46de3c2618508735f1db208064d3be
("inpcom.c: evaluate .param with agauss etc. once, as documented", 2026-10-14,
after ngspice-47), rebased onto ngspice-47 (a80f6e3e) with no change to the
code: the hunks move by -10 lines. A top-level .param with agauss, gauss,
aunif, unif or limit stays a .param, drawn once per circuit load, when every
identifier in its expression is a top-level parameter or function; a .param
inside a .subckt stays a .param (one draw per instance); only the rest becomes
a .func, as before. `set stat_param_as_func` restores the ngspice-47
behaviour. Decision F1 (a) of docs/decisions/m9-decision-table.md (capability
simulation-monte-carlo, "Statistical functions in ngspice (informative)").
Licence: the Modified BSD licence of ngspice, as src/frontend/inpcom.c.
Justification: patches/series.

